{
  "description": "A controlled NextItNet sequential recommendation experiment across four Amazon datasets: Movies_and_TV, Industrial_and_Scientific, Electronics, and CDs_and_Vinyl. Preserve the supplied corrected NextItNet backbone and train one independent model per category. Select changes using macro-average validation HR@10.",
  "motivation": "Measure improvements within the NextItNet family under fixed data splits, seeds, evaluation conditions, and compute limits, without ensemble effects or test-set feedback.",
  "implementation_notes": "Use preprocessing seed 0, training seed 42, at most 200 epochs, and 200 batches per epoch. Keep DATA_DIR = os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'] and save artifacts beneath the trial directory. For left-padded histories, read the final nonpadding position, never count-1. Preserve category routing, the ModelView compatibility interfaces, and the required diagnosis APIs. Update the embedded predictor whenever architecture changes; each category must load exactly one trained checkpoint. Evaluate through the host's pinned validation procedure and respect the shared 43,200 GPU-second search budget. The supplied description contains no baseline source code or measured results, so implementation details and performance cannot be verified.",
  "pseudocode": "set_preprocessing_seed(0)\nfor category in FOUR_CATEGORIES:\n    set_training_seed(42)\n    data = load_supplied_splits(os.environ['GAGC_DATA_DIR'], category)\n    model = supplied_corrected_nextitnet(category)\n    train(model, data.train, max_epochs=200, batches_per_epoch=200)\n    save_one_checkpoint(model, trial_directory, category)\nwrite_matching_predictor_with_category_routing()\n# Host independently measures validation HR@10 per category.\n# Selection objective: arithmetic mean of the four validation HR@10 values.",
  "originality": {
    "score": 2,
    "positive": "Provides a carefully constrained, family-specific baseline for comparable experiments.",
    "negative": "No new architectural mechanism or learning objective is described. Score uses a 1–10 scale."
  },
  "future_potential": {
    "score": 7,
    "positive": "Supports controlled exploration of jointly trained NextItNet layers, losses, sampling, and optimization.",
    "negative": "Potential improvements remain unmeasured and must fit the fixed search budget. Score uses a 1–10 scale."
  },
  "code_difficulty": {
    "score": 6,
    "positive": "The existing corrected baseline should provide the training and inference foundation.",
    "negative": "Architecture changes require synchronized checkpoints, predictor generation, diagnostics, and padding-aware readout. Difficulty uses a 1–10 scale."
  }
}
